{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_61","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'pose suggest review --path pose-mcp'","aggregated_output":"# POSE trail — review\n\nAvaliação técnica de PR/diff: escopo, contratos, segurança, validação.\n- Path:      pose-mcp → domain: backend-go (repo-map)\n- Workflow:  .pose/workflows/review.md\n- Skill:     pose-review\n- Rules:     .pose/rules/security.md, .pose/rules/documentation-style.md, .pose/rules/backend-go.md\n- Spec:      false\n- ADR:       false\n- Knowledge: consume=true, produce=handoff (quando aceitar risco residual ou condicionar merge)\n- Validation: exigir evidência de pose validate do implementador\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_62","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'closeout-review-policy' .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json pose-mcp/internal/cli/testdata/adversarial/README.md POSE.md .pose/templates/roadmap.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_62","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'closeout-review-policy' .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json pose-mcp/internal/cli/testdata/adversarial/README.md POSE.md .pose/templates/roadmap.md\"","aggregated_output":"POSE.md:374:  **Closeout review policy (schema 5):** an instance that adopts `pose adopt closeout-review-policy` decides with `milestone_review_required` and `roadmap_review_required` (`never`, `when-justified`, `always`) whether the close of a milestone or a roadmap owes its own review. `when-justified` requires it for a milestone with more than two distinct specs, and for a roadmap with more than one distinct spec and at least one ADR association (`adrs: [adr:<file>.md]` on the roadmap, `roadmaps: [roadmap:<slug>]` on the ADR, or a local Markdown link either way). `always` requires it even for a one-member milestone, and neither the singleton inheritance nor `unreviewed_milestones` weakens it. Member reviews stay required; a review recorded on the scope anyway is verified as before and its rejection stands; a member or association that cannot be resolved never grants an exemption. A milestone that closes without its own review keeps its exit gate: the gate is carried into the review plan of its only member, or of its last member (the one sealed once every other member is terminal), and the close is blocked until an approved member review judged the gate as it reads now, or the milestone is reviewed itself. A member a transfer moved counts at its destination, and a milestone or roadmap named by `after:`, `consumes:` or a spec's `depends_on` satisfies the edge, and makes a dependent spec ready, only once closed under its project's adopted policy, not by its members' status; a done roadmap closed by its receipt keeps its milestones reachable again if their closure stops verifying. Under the adopted policy `pose close milestone:<roadmap>/<id>` and `pose close roadmap:<slug>` stay explicit in every mode and publish a receipt (`review-closeouts/<milestone|roadmap>/…json` inside `.pose/`) with `review: required|not-required`, the key, the value, `closeout-review@1` and the reason (`members=1, threshold>2`); the scope is terminal only with it. New instances adopt `never`/`never`; an existing policy keeps the legacy rule until it adopts, `pose setup` shows both, `pose doctor` lists open scopes that owe a review, and roadmaps closed before adoption are verified by the contract they were sealed under.\n.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json:2367:          \"name\": \"closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
